      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To determine the required beam size, we can use the formula L/360 to calculate the deflection limit. This means the beam should deflect no more than 1/360 of its length. For your span of 14 feet, that's 0.039 flexural rigidity. Using a static factor for your live and dead loads, we can calculate the required beam diameter. What's the preferred bearing capacity (P/d ratio) and the desired beam strength (moment capacity)?",
